WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.790
One page travels down a
timeline, from 1813 to 2026.

2
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.580
At every stop, the same
opening sentence lights up:

3
00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:12.550
"It is a truth universally acknowledged".

4
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.710
It moves on: a train,
a library, a classroom.

5
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.640
Does it read the same in each?

6
00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:19.950
Same words.

7
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.850
Would they mean the same if they
were written somewhere else, or now?

8
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:27.060
In this mission, you'll
ask what context means:

9
00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:30.420
the moment a text is made,
or the moment it's read?

10
00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:35.340
You'll learn what an entail was: a rule
that kept an estate in the male line.

11
00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:39.490
And you'll imagine the novel in
the hands of a reader in 2026,

12
00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.490
in Lagos or Toronto.

13
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.930
Your mission: decide whether
the work would mean the same.
